@page
@model KopiCinta.Pages.TeamArdisaModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Ardisa Faras Dewi";
}

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">

        <div class="back-top reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Team">← Back</a>
        </div>

        <div class="event-hero reveal">
            <div class="event-hero-text">
                <p class="eyebrow">Our Team</p>
                <h2>Ardisa Faras Dewi</h2>

                <p class="event-intro">
                    A Deaf staff member whose journey at Kopi Cinta began with barista
                    training and grew into a meaningful space for learning, service, and connection.
                </p>

                <div class="event-tags">
                    <span>Deaf Staff</span>
                    <span>Barista</span>
                    <span>Communication Access</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="team-profile-hero-img reveal">
                <img src="/images/team/ardisa.jpg" alt="Ardisa Faras Dewi">
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-block reveal">
            <div class="hbii-block-text">
                <p class="hbii-label">Her Beginning</p>
                <h3>Learning From the Basics</h3>

                <p>
                    Ardisa Faras Dewi started her journey at Kopi Cinta by joining
                    a barista training program for about two weeks.
                </p>

                <p>
                    During the training, she learned everything from the basics until
                    she truly understood the process.
                </p>

                <p>
                    After that, she continued as a Deaf staff member, handling the bar
                    and popcorn service.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-block-card">
                <h4>Her Role</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Deaf staff member</li>
                    <li>Bar service</li>
                    <li>Popcorn service</li>
                    <li>SOP and recipe practice</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-feature reveal">
            <div class="hbii-feature-card">
                <p class="hbii-label">Growth</p>
                <h3>Finding More Than Experience</h3>

                <p>
                    At first, Ardisa simply wanted to gain new experience in the working
                    world and business.
                </p>

                <p>
                    She learned how to follow SOPs, understand recipes, and work within
                    a structured system.
                </p>

                <p>
                    But over time, she found something more meaningful through the process.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-feature-card soft">
                <p class="hbii-label">Belonging</p>
                <h3>Comfort in the Workplace</h3>

                <p>
                    Ardisa feels comfortable working at Kopi Cinta. Even though she sometimes
                    feels tired, she still goes through it happily.
                </p>

                <p>
                    For her, being here feels meaningful because she is part of a team
                    and a space that continues to help her learn and grow.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-block reveal">
            <div class="hbii-block-text">
                <p class="hbii-label">Challenge</p>
                <h3>When Communication Takes More Effort</h3>

                <p>
                    As a Deaf person, Ardisa’s biggest challenge is communication.
                    She often relies on lip-reading, which can be difficult when people
                    speak too fast.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Even so, she continues to learn, adapt, and find ways to understand
                    and be understood.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-highlight-panel">
                <div>
                    <strong>Writing</strong>
                    <span>Helps make information clearer.</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong>Gestures</strong>
                    <span>Supports everyday communication.</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong>Sign Language</strong>
                    <span>Creates better access for Deaf individuals.</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-ending reveal">
            <h3>Her Hope</h3>

            <p>
                Through her experience, Ardisa hopes hearing people can become more aware
                of the importance of communication access for Deaf individuals.
            </p>

            <p>
                Whether through writing, gestures, or sign language, every effort can help
                make communication more inclusive.
            </p>

            <p>
                Because for her, access is not just about understanding words—
                but about making sure no one is left out of the conversation.
            </p>
        </div>

        <br />

        <div class="detail-back reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Team" class="btn btn-secondary">← Back to Team</a>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>